# Packages that move out of the per-board image build and into the drop.
#
# One name per line, matching the package name buildroot uses in
# build/packages-file-list.txt (which is the package directory name).  A name
# that is not enabled for the board being harvested is skipped, so this file is
# the union over every board on the ABI, not a per-board list.
#
# A package enabled on only some boards (ioquake3 is h700-only) belongs here
# too: harvest skips what a board did not build, and the drop is the union over
# the ABI.  Deriving this list from one board's build is what missed it.
#
# Note that some packages sit one level deeper than the emulator family that
# names them -- openbor/openbor6412, mupen64plus/mupen64plus-core,
# easyrpg/easyrpg-player -- so a directory name is not always a package name.
# harvest-drop.py walks both levels when it reports candidates missing from here.
#
# Membership is explicit rather than "everything under emulators/ and ports/"
# on purpose: what belongs in the drop is a decision about build time and
# stability, and a glob would silently swallow a package the moment someone
# adds a directory.  harvest-drop.py warns about candidates that are installed
# but not listed here, so new packages get noticed instead of missed.
#
# Their dependencies are NOT listed.  harvest-drop.py works out which
# dependency packages exist only because of these ones and carries those too;
# anything shared with the rest of the image keeps being built normally.
#
# retroarch is deliberately absent: the cores plug into it, so it stays in the
# image build where it versions together with them.
#
# python-pygame2 and hypseus-singe are absent for a different reason:
# the knulli gate cannot switch them off, because they are also selected from
# inside the batocera submodule (batocera-pygame, batocera-wine,
# hypseus-singe-bezels).  Listing them would put them in the drop AND keep
# compiling them per board.  Gating them means patching upstream first; until
# then they cost 1.1 and 0.9 minutes respectively.
#
# Some entries below are not emulators but companions private to one: a package
# that exists only to serve a single emulator and is selected by it, never by
# the image.  They ride in the drop rather than the base for the same reason the
# emulator does -- nothing else would keep them alive once it is gone.

# --- standalone emulators ---
advanced_drastic
amiberry
amiberry-lite
azahar
dolphin-emu
dosbox-staging
dosbox-x
dsperate
flycast
gsplus
hatari
easyrpg-player
lexaloffle-pico8
mupen64plus-audio-sdl
mupen64plus-core
mupen64plus-input-sdl
mupen64plus-rsp-hle
mupen64plus-ui-console
mupen64plus-video-glide64mk2
mupen64plus-video-rice
openbor4432
openbor6412
openbor7142
openbor7530
lightspark
ppsspp
scummvm
simcoupe
solarus-engine
thextech
vice
vita3k
x16emu

# --- ports / game engines ---
abuse
corsixth
cannonball
cdogs
cgenius
devilutionx
eduke32
fallout1-ce
fallout2-ce
gzdoom
hcl
hurrican
ioquake3
iortcw
openjazz
raze
sdlpop
taradino
tyrian

# --- companions private to one of the above ---
#
# (the '#keep' section at the end of this file is not part of the drop)
sdl2_drastic        # advanced_drastic's private SDL2
drastic_layout      # advanced_drastic's layout data
liblcf              # easyrpg-player's format library
lpeg                # corsixth lua modules, loaded by require() at runtime,
luafilesystem       # so they never show up in a NEEDED list
luasec
luasocket

# --- deliberately NOT in the drop ---
#
# These sit under an emulator directory, so harvest-drop.py sees them as
# candidates, but they belong in the base image.  Listing them here as '#keep'
# records the decision and keeps the "installed but not in emulators.set"
# warning meaningful: anything the warning still names is a package nobody has
# ruled on yet.
#
# Libraries the emulators need but that are libraries, not emulators.  These are
# in BR2_PACKAGE_KNULLI_EXTERNAL_EMULATORS's select list precisely so the image
# keeps building them once the emulators are gone -- putting them in the drop
# instead would ship a second copy that could drift from the image's.
#keep batocera-luajit
#keep iir
#keep libenet
#keep libjpeg-bato
#keep libportmidi
#
# Wanted by the rest of the image on their own merits (retroarch, kodi,
# configgen), so they would be built per board whether the emulators were here
# or not.
#keep batocera-retroachievements-sounds
#keep ecm
#keep ffmpeg-python
#keep ffmpeg-rockchip
#keep ffmpeg4
#keep libcapsimage
#keep libgraphene
#keep libplacebo
#keep libretro-core-info
#keep libxmp
#keep python-hidapi
#keep python3-configobj
#keep sdl12-compat
#keep sdl3
#keep sdl3_image
#keep wildmidi
#
# Needs Qt6, and Qt6 is 112MB of libraries no other board on the ABI has any use
# for.  Only rk3576 selects it here, so the drop would gain nothing and charge
# h700, a133 and rk3326 for a Qt stack to run a binary they cannot use.  It is a
# prebuilt binary, so leaving it per-board costs no compile time.
#keep aethersx2
#
# Emulators that cannot be gated: also selected from inside the batocera
# submodule (batocera-pygame, batocera-wine, hypseus-singe-bezels), so the knulli
# gate cannot switch them off.  Listing them in the drop would put them in the
# payload AND keep compiling them per board.  Gating them means patching
# upstream first; until then they cost 1.1 and 0.9 minutes respectively.
#keep hypseus-singe
#keep python-pygame2
#
# sonic2013/soniccd: RSDKv4 1.3.3 needs libglew (xorg+libGL only) and batocera
# dropped the legacy no-glew revision, so they build on no board here.  Not
# listed at all -- a name in this file must have payload in the drop.
